Gaussian basis set library
==========================

377 basis sets (*.BAS, with *.BAS.meta descriptors), served by the ECCE
data server as Ecce/system/GaussianBasisSetLibrary and loaded through
EDSIGaussianBasisSetLibrary.

Why this data ships
-------------------
It is not a convenience.  ECCE writes basis sets INTO the generated input
deck as explicit exponents and coefficients rather than naming the
computational code's built-in library: TGBSConfig::dump() always emits a
NumericalBasis section, and the NameBasis section is an optional addition
suppressed for any "Custom" or "Imported" configuration, for any basis
listed in data/client/config/BasisSetUseExp, and for any basis the user
has uncontracted, appended functions to, or deleted contractions from.
Those operations cannot be expressed as a library name at all.

So without this data ECCE cannot produce a basis set -- not even by name,
since the selection UI is driven by what the library contains.

Provenance
----------
Exported from the EMSL Basis Set Exchange (the retired bse.pnl.gov), 2013
to 2015.  Each descriptor records its own export stamp on line 17, e.g.

    pc-1  EMSL  Basis Set Exchange Library  6/19/15 6:31 AM

That site has been retired and redirects to basissetexchange.org, so the
terms under which these particular exports were made are not recoverable
from it.  The successor project (MolSSI) publishes its repository under
the BSD 3-Clause license; note that the licence statement covers "the
project" and does not separately address the basis set data, so it should
not be read here as a settled statement about redistribution.  Anyone
needing certainty should ask MolSSI (bse@molssi.org).

See issue #116.

Citation
--------
Cite the literature reference for the basis set itself -- each .BAS and
.BAS.meta file carries its own references section -- and the Basis Set
Exchange:

  D. Feller, J. Comp. Chem. 17(13), 1571-1586 (1996).
  K.L. Schuchardt, B.T. Didier, T. Elsethagen, L. Sun, V. Gurumoorthi,
    J. Chase, J. Li, T.L. Windus, J. Chem. Inf. Model. 47(3), 1045-1052
    (2007).

For anything obtained from the present Basis Set Exchange, cite instead:

  B.P. Pritchard, D. Altarawy, B.T. Didier, T.D. Gibson, T.L. Windus,
    J. Chem. Inf. Model. 59(11), 4814-4820 (2019).
